We are looking for volunteers who are willing to generate and maintain
ready-to-use packages for individual Linux distributions.

Future target: support a 386 with a 387 floating point coprocessor.
The current i386 runtime requires a Pentium because small allocations use
CMPXCHG8B. Replace that fast path with Storage.AllocateWithTag, check
allocation during startup and signal handling, and rebuild the runtime
and bootstrap compilers. Keep x87 floating point and HUGEINT DIV/MOD;
a processor without a floating point coprocessor is a separate target.
